      "outputTokens": 1342,
      "costUsd": 0.012171,
      "pronunciationText": "The trouble is the second minus sign. Think of the thermometer. At six it read minus two degrees, and at nine it read one degree. It warmed by one, minus, bracket, minus two, which is three degrees, not one minus two. F of a works the same way. F of a means the primitive at the lower limit, the start. Here that's F of minus two, which is minus eight thirds, a negative number, and the rule subtracts the whole of it. So put F of a in its own brackets, every time. One third, minus, bracket, minus eight thirds. Subtracting a negative adds, so that's one third plus eight thirds, which is three. Positive, as the picture said. The minus sign in the rule belongs to the subtraction. The minus sign inside F of a belongs to the number. Keep them apart, and neither gets lost."
    },
