      "inputTokens": 179,
      "outputTokens": 1281,
      "costUsd": 0.011618499999999999,
      "pronunciationText": "We can check that three another way. Split the region at zero. From minus two to zero, the integral is zero, minus, bracket, minus eight thirds, which is eight thirds. From zero to one, it's one third minus zero, which is one third. Eight thirds plus one third is three, the same answer. The thermometer does the same thing, two degrees up to zero, then one more. That always works, for a continuous function. The integral from a to b, plus the integral from b to c, is the integral from a to c, when b is between them. In primitives, that's F of b minus F of ay, plus F of c minus F of b. The middle value cancels, so you're left with F of c minus F of ay. On the graph, two regions side by side make one region."
