      "pronunciationText": "The rule also runs backwards. Find k, with k greater than one, so that the integral from one to k of two x equals eight. A primitive of two x is x squared, so the integral is k squared, minus one squared. Set k squared minus one equal to eight. Then k squared is nine, so k is three, or minus three. Now the sign check. Minus three fits the equation too, because the integral from one down to minus three is a backwards integral, and it comes out as plus eight as well. But the question says k is greater than one, so k equals three."
